  "question": {
    "text": "The speed of a wave produced in water is given by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#957;</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>&#955;</mi><mi>a</mi></msup><msup><mi>g</mi><mi>b</mi></msup><msup><mi>&#961;</mi><mi>c</mi></msup></math>. Where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>g</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#961;</mi></math> are wavelength of wave, acceleration due to gravity and density of water respectively. The values of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>b</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>c</mi></math> respectively, are"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>0</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>0</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>0</mn></math>",
